    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d565">

                <pb facs="0690" n="622" sameAs="frus:frus1867p1/pg622"/>

                <head>Mr. Sanford to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 413.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United States</hi>,
                                <hi rendition="#italic">Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1867-03-12"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >March</hi> 12, 1867.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: What remains of the Belgian legion in
                    Mexico disembarked from the French transport Rhone on the 9th at Antwerp, in
                    number 780 men. Of the remainder 200 were killed or disappeared, and the others
                    have been invalided or left behind. They were received in public barracks at
                    Antwerp, and those who need it are aided by the government to return to their
                    homes.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with great respect, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>H. S. SANFORD.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William H. Seward</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Secretary of State, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
